{"question_text": {"স্পেশাল বিসিএস (স্বাস্থ্য) - লং কোর্স": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Which of the following cytoplasmic organelles is not involved in protein synthesis? ", "option1": "Rough endoplasmic reticulum ", "option2": "Mitochondria ", "option3": "Golgi apparatus ", "option4": "Ribosome ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<u><strong>Cytoplasmic organelles Involved in Protein Synthesis (Translation):</strong></u><br />1. Ribosome<br />2. RER<br />3. Mitochondria<br /><br /><u><strong>Post-translational Modification of Protein Occurs in:</strong></u><br />1. Golgi apparatus<br />2. Ribosome<br />3. RER"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) The inner mitochondrial membrane is a site for-", "option1": "β-oxidation of fatty acids ", "option2": "Electron transport chain", "option3": "Ketogenesis", "option4": "Citric acid cycle ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<u><strong>Functions of mitochondria:</strong></u><br />1. Production of ATP by aerobic respiration<br />2. Mitochondrial DNA takes part in RNA &amp; protein synthesis<br />3. Role in cellular catabolism by apoptosis (programmed cell death)<br /><strong>4. Mitochondria contains enzymes that take part in-</strong><br />&nbsp; &nbsp;a. Respiratory chain or electron transport<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;b. Oxidative phosphorylation<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;c. Krebs/citric acid cycle<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;d. &beta;-oxidation of fatty acid<br />&nbsp; &nbsp;e. Ketogenesis<br /><br />Inner mitochondrial membrane shows long infoldings called cristae (for increasing surface area).<br />The lipid bilayer of the inner membrane contains unusual phospholipids and is highly impermeable to ions.<br />Inner mitochondrial membrane is a<em><strong> site for oxidative phosphorylation, respiratory (electron transport) chain, and ATP synthesis.<br /><br /></strong></em>[Ref. Junquiera 15th, 39]"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) Intermediate filaments present in muscle cells-", "option1": "Cytokeratin ", "option2": "Synemin ", "option3": "Peripherin ", "option4": "Vimentin ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<sup><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/intermediate_filaments_NFk2GI0.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"611\" /><br /><br />[Ref, Junqueira 15th, 47]&nbsp;</sup>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) Microtubules are present in-", "option1": "Mitotic spindles ", "option2": "Microvilli ", "option3": "Gap junctions ", "option4": "Nuclear envelope", "answer": "1", "exp": "Microtubules are non branching hollow tubules made up of tubulin proteins (&alpha; and b tubulin) with a diameter of 25 nm<br /><br /><u><strong>Locations:</strong></u><br />&bull; Cilia<br />&bull; Flagella<br />&bull; Centrioles<br />&bull; Mitotic spindle<br />&bull; Elongating cell processes and<br />&bull; Growing axons<br /><br /><u><strong>Functions:</strong></u><br />1. Movement of cilia, flagella (tail of sperm)<br />2. Intracellular transport of vesicles<br />3. In cell division, formation of mitotic spindle<br />4. Maintenance of cell shape<br /><br />[Ref. Junquira 15th, 43]"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Nucleus is absent in-", "option1": "Normoblasts ", "option2": "Keratinocytes ", "option3": "Odontoblasts ", "option4": "Platelets ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<u><strong>Most of the cells contain single nucleus except-</strong></u><br />&ndash; <em><strong>RBCs and platelets do not have nuclei</strong></em><br />&ndash; Striated muscle cells are multinucleated<br />&ndash; Few hepatocytes and transitional epithelial cells are binucleated<br /><br />*** Normoblasts have nucleus, after this stage, they loss their nuclei to become reticulocytes, and the mature RBCs.&nbsp;"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) DNA replication occurs during which phase of cell cycle? ", "option1": "Mitosis", "option2": "G1 phase", "option3": "G2 phase ", "option4": "S phase ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cell_Cycle_MHs_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"550\" /><br /><br />[Ref. Junquira 15th, 62]"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Epithelial cells are bound to the basal lamina by-", "option1": "Hemidesmosomes ", "option2": "Tight junctions ", "option3": "Zonulae adherens ", "option4": "Desmosomes ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Intercellular_Adhesions_2_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"528\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Intercellular_adhesions_Fig.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"631\" />"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Which is an example of tubuloacinar gland? ", "option1": "Eccrine sweat gland", "option2": "Exocrine pancreas", "option3": "Parotid gland ", "option4": "Brunner's gland", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Glands_Junqueira_LRJg8Sp.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"866\" height=\"755\" /><br /><br />[Ref. Junqueira 15th, 89]"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) All of the followings are resident cell of the connective tissue except-", "option1": "Adipocytes ", "option2": "Macrophages", "option3": "Mast cells", "option4": "Plasma cells", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/connective_tissue_cells.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"389\" />"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) The Howship's lacunae contain-", "option1": "Osteoprogenitor cells", "option2": "Osteoclasts ", "option3": "Osteoblasts ", "option4": "Osteocytes ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/bone_cells_lauvV9l.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"842\" height=\"316\" />"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) Elastic cartilage is present in-", "option1": "Menisci of knee", "option2": "Arytenoid cartilage ", "option3": "Corniculate cartilage", "option4": "Epiphysis", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cartilage_locations_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"501\" />"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) Lymphoid nodules are absent in-", "option1": "Thymus ", "option2": "Spleen ", "option3": "Lymph nodes", "option4": "Vermiform appendix", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/lymphoid_organs_difference_v0us5og.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"571\" /><br /><br />[Ref. Junqueira 15th]&nbsp;"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) Bipolar neurons are present in-", "option1": "Pyramidal cells ", "option2": "Vestibulocochlear ganglia ", "option3": "Mesencephalic nucleus ", "option4": "Dorsal root ganglia", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/neuron_classification_gm7ERdA.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"470\" />"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) Blood brain barrier is formed by-", "option1": "Ependymal cells ", "option2": "Oligodendrocytes ", "option3": "Choroid epithelial cells", "option4": "Astrocytes ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Glial_cells_1_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"586\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Glial_cells_2_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"438\" />"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Which is not true regarding skeletal muscle fibres? ", "option1": "cells are multinucleated ", "option2": "have prominent cross striation ", "option3": "have gap junctions between the cells", "option4": "have well developed sarcoplasmic reticulum", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/muscle_tissue_qKspMr1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"629\" /><br />[Ref. Junqueira 15th]&nbsp;"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Which of the followings is not a neural crest derivative? ", "option1": "Adrenal medulla ", "option2": "Anterior pituitary ", "option3": "Arachnoid matter ", "option4": "Melanocyte ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<em><strong>Rathke's pouch and anterior pituitary develop from stomatodaeum (surface ectoderm)</strong></em>&nbsp;<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/neuroectoderm_mhs_eXM9AMM.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"505\" />"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) The female urethra develops mainly from- ", "option1": "Mesonephric duct ", "option2": "Primitive urogenital sinus", "option3": "Paramesonephric duct ", "option4": "Proctodaeum ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Cloaca_P1yt0qM.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"569\" />"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) The fetal umbilical vein persists as-", "option1": "Ligamentum venosum ", "option2": "Ligamentum teres hepatis", "option3": "Median umbilical ligament", "option4": "Medial umbilical ligament ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/remnants_dNkp3Aj.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"436\" />"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) The third pharyngeal pouch gives rise to-", "option1": "Inferior parathyroid glands ", "option2": "Crypts of palatine tonsil ", "option3": "Superior parathyroid glands ", "option4": "Ultimobranchial body ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Pharyngeal_pouch__cleft_MHS_Q25GpHT.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"527\" />"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) All are derivatives of the endodermal foregut, except-", "option1": "Liver ", "option2": "Stomach ", "option3": "Spleen ", "option4": "Gall bladder ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<em><strong>Spleen develops from the mesoderm.&nbsp;<br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Primitive_gut_derivatives_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"591\" /><br /></strong></em>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Which is the artery of cerebral hemorrhage? ", "option1": "Lateral striate artery ", "option2": "Anterior choroidal artery ", "option3": "Posterior communicating artery ", "option4": "Medial striate artery ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/intracranial_hemorrhage_K1sHzpd.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"844\" /><br />[Ref. Vishram Sinmgh Clinical Neuroanatomy]"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Choroid plexus is absent in-", "option1": "Floor of the lateral ventricle ", "option2": "Roof of the third ventricle", "option3": "Occipital horn of lateral ventricle", "option4": "Roof of fourth ventricle", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Choroid_plexus_MHS_qLYAX6Q.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"618\" />"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) All of the followings are motor nuclei of the cranial nerves, except-", "option1": "Spinal nucleus of accessory nerve", "option2": "Edinger-Westphal nucleus", "option3": "Superior salivatory nucleus ", "option4": "Nucleus tractus solitarius ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cranial_nerve_nuclei_mhs_al0rC6C.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"564\" />"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) The circle of Willis does not receive contribution from-", "option1": "Internal carotid artery ", "option2": "Middle cerebral artery ", "option3": "Posterior cerebral artery ", "option4": "Anterior cerebral artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Circle_of_Willis_MHS_KtmUCzK.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"639\" /><br />[Ref. Snell's Cilinical Neuroanatomy]&nbsp;"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) A lesion affecting the Broca's area of the brain will result in-", "option1": "Astereognosis", "option2": "Expressive aphasia ", "option3": "Sensory aphasia ", "option4": "Extrapyramidal symptoms ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Fronta__parietal_lobe_Oa1w8OL.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"826\" /><br /><br />[Ref. BD Chaurasia 4th Vol.]"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) Which is not a part of the basal ganglia? ", "option1": "Putamen ", "option2": "Red nucleus ", "option3": "Amygdaloid nucleus ", "option4": "Caudate nucleus ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Basal_ganglia_mhs_9tyxwMW.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"590\" />"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) Diagnosis of brainstem death does not require testing-", "option1": "Respiratory drive", "option2": "Corneal reflex ", "option3": "Gag reflex ", "option4": "Hoffmann's sign ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Brainstem_death_fqBa8Mc.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1320\" height=\"1244\" />"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) Which is a non-capsulated receptor? ", "option1": "Meissner corpuscle", "option2": "Merkel cell", "option3": "Krause end bulb ", "option4": "Pacinian corpuscle", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Receptors_in_skin_C2Er1hF.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"718\" />"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Taste sensation from the vallate papilla is carried by the-", "option1": "Lingual nerve ", "option2": "Chorda tympani ", "option3": "Glossopharyngeal nerve ", "option4": "Vagus nerve ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Tongue_Table_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"616\" /><br /><br />[Ref. BD Chaurasia Vol.3]&nbsp;"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) Which of the following movements of the eyeball will be affected in abducent nerve injury? ", "option1": "Abduction ", "option2": "Adduction ", "option3": "Elevation ", "option4": "Extorsion ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<em><strong>Abducent nerve supplies the lateral rectus.&nbsp;</strong></em><br /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Extraocular_muscle_action_ZS8SiRP.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"263\" />"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) Which is the largest of the cerebellar nuclei? ", "option1": "Dentate nucleus ", "option2": "Emboliform nucleus ", "option3": "Globose nucleus ", "option4": "Fastigial nucleus ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/cerebellum_nuclei.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1203\" />"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) Lateral medullary syndrome results from occlusion of-", "option1": "Anterior spinal artery ", "option2": "Posterior inferior cerebellar artery ", "option3": "Posterior cerebral artery ", "option4": "Posterior spinal artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Lateral_medullary_syndrome_MHS_wRAx6g6.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"590\" />"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) Inferior meatus of the nose receives the opening of-", "option1": "Sphenoidal air sinus ", "option2": "Maxillary sinus ", "option3": "Posterior ethmoidal air sinus", "option4": "Nasolacrimal duct ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/meatus_opening_5VCexUg.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"321\" />"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) Which is a branch of the lateral cord of the brachial plexus? ", "option1": "Axillary nerve ", "option2": "Musculocutaneous nerve ", "option3": "Thoracodorsal nerve ", "option4": "Suprascapular nerve ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Brachial_plexus_MqCCqii.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1061\" />"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) Which is the independent sensory area of the radial nerve in the hand? ", "option1": "Dorsal aspect of lateral three and half digits ", "option2": "Tip of the thumb ", "option3": "Base of the thumb over the dorsal aspect", "option4": "Palmar aspect of lateral three and half digits ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Sensory_supply_of_hand_BL.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"549\" />"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) Which is not true regarding the right ventricle? ", "option1": "has moderator band ", "option2": "crescentic in cross section", "option3": "forms majority of the sternocostal surface", "option4": "has two papillary muscles", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Ventricles_difference_Q08aM7o.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"467\" /><br /><br />[Ref. BD Chaurasia Vol.1]&nbsp;"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) Conducting system of the heart is made up of-", "option1": "Nerve fibres ", "option2": "Myocardium ", "option3": "Endocardium ", "option4": "Epicardium ", "answer": "2", "exp": "The conducting system is <strong><em>made up of specialized</em> myocardium (not nervous tissue)</strong><br /><br />Its fibres are finer than other myocardial fibres and are completely cross striated<br /><br /><u><strong>Parts:</strong></u><br />1. Sinoatrial node (SA node)<br />2. Atrioventricular node (AV node)<br />3. Atrioventricular bundle (of His)<br />4. Right and left branches of AV bundle<br />5. Sub endocardial Purkinje fibres<br /><br /><u><strong>Blood supply:</strong></u> <br />Whole of conducting system except left branch of AV bundle is supplied by right coronary artery. In 40% cases, left coronary artery supplies SA node.&nbsp;"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) The thoracic duct receives lymph from-", "option1": "Right upper limb ", "option2": "Right lung ", "option3": "Right breast ", "option4": "Right lower limb ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Thoracic_duct_drainage_area.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"847\" height=\"1192\" />"}, {"id": "39", "question": "৩৯) Which of the followings is not a branch of the external carotid artery? ", "option1": "Maxillary artery ", "option2": "Inferior thyroid artery ", "option3": "Ascending pharyngeal artery ", "option4": "Superior thyroid artery ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/External_carotid_artery_mhs_gdMzChA.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"606\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/External_carotid_fig.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"908\" />"}, {"id": "40", "question": "৪০) Which is the most dependent part of the lungs in supine position? ", "option1": "Superior segment of lower lobe ", "option2": "Posterior segment of upper lobe ", "option3": "Lateral segment of middle lobe ", "option4": "Posterior basal segment of lower lobe ", "answer": "1", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/bronchopulmonary_Segments_Importance_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"407\" />"}, {"id": "41", "question": "৪১) Muscle acting during forced expiration-", "option1": "Serratus posterior superior ", "option2": "External intercostal ", "option3": "Quadratus lumborum ", "option4": "Levator scapulae ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Muscles_of_respiration_J87S1r9.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"766\" />"}, {"id": "42", "question": "৪২) Aortic opening of the diaphragm transmits-", "option1": "Left phrenic nerve ", "option2": "Left vagal trunk ", "option3": "Hemiazygos vein ", "option4": "Thoracic duct ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Diaphragm_Major_Openings_MHS.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"625\" />"}, {"id": "43", "question": "৪৩) Which is the 'safety muscle' of the larynx? ", "option1": "Cricothyroid ", "option2": "Posterior cricoarytenoid ", "option3": "Lateral cricoarytenoid ", "option4": "Oblique arytenoid ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/safety_muscle_of_larynx.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"238\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/larynx_muscles_ZIvgZaw.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"569\" />"}, {"id": "44", "question": "৪৪) Lymphatics from the breast first drains into-", "option1": "Internal mammary nodes", "option2": "Apical group of axillary nodes ", "option3": "Medial group of axillary nodes ", "option4": "Anterior group of axillary nodes ", "answer": "4", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Breast_lymph_drainage_LMCQ_xTOYMJO.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"728\" />"}, {"id": "45", "question": "৪৫) False capsule of the thyroid gland is derived from the-", "option1": "Prevertebral fascia ", "option2": "Investing layer of deep cervical fascia ", "option3": "Pretracheal fascia ", "option4": "Carotid sheath ", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Deep_cervical_fascia.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1556\" />"}, {"id": "46", "question": "৪৬) Which is not true regarding the deep inguinal ring? ", "option1": "is a defect in the fascia transversalis", "option2": "is oval in shape ", "option3": "transmits the ilioinguinal nerve", "option4": "lies lateral to the inferior epigastric artery", "answer": "3", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Inguinal_Rings_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"624\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Inguinal_Rings_Contents_MHS_.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"608\" />"}, {"id": "47", "question": "৪৭) Medial compartment of the femoral sheath contains-", "option1": "Femoral artery ", "option2": "Lymphatic tissue ", "option3": "Femoral vein ", "option4": "Femoral nerve ", "answer": "2", "exp": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/Femoral_sheath_mhs_DGayU39.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"1200\" height=\"605\" /><br /><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-f